        "parms": "# borax — note statistics\nborax measures a stream of notes. A pitch with a velocity other than 0 is a note-on, with 0 a note-off. It does not pass the notes on, so wire it beside the path they take. Its nine outlets, left to right: the note's number, its voice, how many notes sound, pitch, velocity, how many notes have ended, the duration of the note that ended, how many delta times were reported, and the delta time, the time since the previous note-on. Not every outlet fires each time, and the note number goes out last.\nMax's borax reports durations and delta times as whole milliseconds. Here they are floats, precise to a fraction of a millisecond.",
        "type": ".text"
